Dockerfile
============================================================
FROM golang:1.24 AS build
WORKDIR /src
COPY . .
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="-s -w" -o /out/api ./cmd/api

FROM gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12

COPY --from=build /out/api /app/api

WORKDIR /
EXPOSE 8000
ENTRYPOINT ["/app/api"]
============================================================
README.md
============================================================
# Notes

Generated by [CIaC](https://github.com/jrcalgo/ciac) — do not edit the
compiler-owned wiring by hand; regenerate it from the `.ciac` source
instead. Business logic lives in `internal/services/`, which is yours.

## Run

```sh
go run ./cmd/api
```

Or bring up the full stack (API, Postgres, Redis):

```sh
docker compose up --build
```

## Layout

| Path | Purpose | Owner |
|------|---------|-------|
| `cmd/api/main.go` | Application assembly | compiler |
| `internal/routes/` | HTTP handlers (one per api) | compiler |
| `internal/services/` | Business-logic handlers | **you** |
| `internal/workers/` | Queue consumers and scheduled jobs | compiler |
| `internal/config/` | Environment-driven settings | compiler |

Requests to protected routes need a bearer token signed with
`JWT_SECRET` (default `change-me`, algorithm HS256).
